doc Bitwise-or assignment: x |= y, short for x = x | y.
  ```
  let flags = 1
  flags |= 4
  print flags       // 5
  ```

  The left side can be any place of type `int`: a variable, a field, a
  slice element or `*p`, evaluated once.

needs std/let std/addr std/deref std/assign std/bor
syntax statement
  {x: place int} |= {y: expr int}
expand
  let {$p} = &{x}
  *{$p} = *{$p} | {y}
